: "Julia Pfeiffer Burns SP", "Description": "Julia Pfeiffer Burns State Park stretches from the Big Sur coastline into nearby 3,000-foot ridges. The park features redwood, tan oak, madrone, chaparral, and an 80-foot waterfall that drops from granite cliffs into the The park also has a 1,680-acre underwater reserve which protects a spectacular assortment of marine life. Special-use permits allow experienced divers to explore the reserve. Seals, sea lions and sea otters can be seen in the park's cove. Hikers can discover the park's backcountry via several trail systems.  There is no park kiosk at Julia Pfeiffer Burns State Park for fee collection. Campers should register at Pfeiffer Big Sur State Park or Big Sur Station.  For Special Events in the parks such as weddings and small celebrations, please e-mail Special Events at BigSurEvents@parks.ca.gov.", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=578", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/661.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 36.15892586, "Longitude": -121.6704589, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:21", "MilesFromSelected": 77, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 690, "Name": "Pfeiffer Big Sur SP", "Description": "Pfeiffer Big Sur State Park has 1,346 acres of redwood, oak, chaparral, and meadow areas.  Hikers can enjoy 8 miles of hiking trails within the park and over 200 miles of trails in the Ventana Wilderness (USFS) which borders the park.  Overlooks provide views of the Big Sur Valley and the Big Sur River Gorge.  There is no coastal access from this park. ", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Lodging<br>Picnic area<br>Store-convenience<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=570", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/690.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 36.25305556, "Longitude": -121.7811111, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:21", "MilesFromSelected": 86, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 1077, "Name": "Andrew Molera SP", "Description": "Andrew Molera SP", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=582", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/1077.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 36.28840486, "Longitude": -121.844013, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:21", "MilesFromSelected": 90, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 2, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 630, "Name": "Colonel Allensworth SHP", "Description": "Colonel Allensworth State Historic Park is the only California town to be founded, financed and governed by African Americans. The small farming community was founded in 1908 by Colonel Allen Allensworth and a group dedicated to improving the economic and social status of African Americans.  Uncontrollable circumstances, including a drop in the area's water table, resulted in the town's demise. With continuing restoration and special even the town is coming back to ", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=583", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/630.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.86390498, "Longitude": -119.3921095, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:21", "MilesFromSelected": 93, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 3, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 6, "Name": "Carpinteria SB", "Description": "If you are interested in having a RV delivered and set up on your campsite at Carpinteria SB, El Capitan SB, Gaviota SP, or Refugio SB Campgrounds, the following Concessionaire is the approved contract provider: 101 RV Rentals (805) 210-7391. No business or private party may conduct business on State Park property without an approved contract.  Twelve miles south of Santa Barbara, Carpinteria State Beach offers a mile of beach for swimming, surf fishing, tidepool exploring and camping. The Spanish named the area Carpinteria because the Chumash tribe, which lived in the area, had a large seagoing canoe-building enterprise, or &quot;carpentry shop&quot; there. The tribe had chosen the location because of naturally-occurring surface tar which was used to seal the boats.  Seals and sea lions can be seen in the area December through May, as well as an occasional gray whale.  Tidepools contain starfish, sea anemones, crabs, snails, octopi and sea urchin.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>Playground<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=599", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/6.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 34.39246482, "Longitude": -119.5210224, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:21", "MilesFromSelected": 98, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 2, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities":